-*- Mode: Text; -*-

		      ABCL/R2 Installation Guide
			     Aug. 4, 1992
			     Sep. 4, 1998

This document describes how to make ABCL/R2 system on KCl, AKCl,
CMU-CL, and Allegro-CL.

======================================================================
|* Note to the `Allegro CL 5.0beta for Linux' users.
| 
| In the distributed image of ACL5.0beta, the `case mode' is set to
| `:case-sensitive-lower'.  To compile ABCL/R2 system, you have to
| change this to `:case-insensitive-upper'.  Follow the instructions in
| doc/casefaq.txt in the ACL distribution directory, and create a new
| image in which the case mode is :case-insensitive-upper before
| compiling ABCL/R2 system.
======================================================================

1. Specify your environment

1.1.  The Makefile
	Edit the values of variables LISP and BIN to meet your
environment.  For example, if you are using CMU-CL, and want to store
binary files of ABCL/R2 at /home/users/foo/bin, these values would be:
	LISP	= lisp
	BIN	= /home/users/foo/bin
where `lisp' is an executable name of CMU-CL.

1.2. File `src/defabclr2.lsp'
	Edit the default value of variable `*default-abclr2-library-
pathnames*' to contian the default library direcotry of ABCL/R2.  For
example, it would be:
	(defvar *default-abclr2-library-pathnames*
	  (list "" "/usr/local/src/abclr2/lib/"))
where `/usr/local/src/abclr2/lib' is a directory where the default
library programs are stored.  (A nullstring at the first element of
the list means run-time current directory.)

2. Compile
	Type "make", then the system is compiled. After the
compilation, you have "saved_abclr2", which is dumped image of the
system, at "src" directory.

3. Install
	Type `make install-kcl' (for KCl and AKCl user), `make
install-cmu' (for CMU-CL user), or `make install-acl' (for Allegro-CL
user) then you have a file named `abclr2' at a directory pointed by
the value of `BIN' in Makeflie.

4. Run
	Execute `abclr2' just created.  Enjoy.

